cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Helix in published work, please cite it as below, and cite the
  source databases and methods your results depend on. Each project's
  Methods export in Helix lists exactly which ones those are.
title: "Helix: a unified bioinformatics workspace"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-12"
authors:
  - name: secretcoder45
repository-code: "https://github.com/secretcoder45/Helix"
url: "https://get-helix.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  Helix resolves a gene or protein across UniProtKB, NCBI Gene, RCSB PDB,
  KEGG and AlphaFold DB in one lookup, and provides pairwise alignment
  (Needleman–Wunsch, Smith–Waterman), phylogeny, protein and DNA analysis,
  restriction mapping and primer design. Saved results record the source
  database release, entry version and sequence checksum they came from.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - sequence alignment
  - UniProt
  - reproducibility
